          "date": "2026-11-11 06:29:25.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 kunit: add optional gcov coverage to ku",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 kunit: add optional gcov coverage to ku\n\nAdd support to measure test coverage.\n\n-g requires CONFIG_GCOV_KERNEL, debugfs mounted, root, and the gcov\nand gcov-tool binaries from the matching gcc; it is off by default\nsince not every test setup has that kernel config.\n\nku resets the kernel's gcov counters before each module is inserted,\nand after the test run (before rmmod, since counters vanish then)\ncopies the .gcda files out of debugfs next to the matching .gcno/.c,\nmerging them (summing counts) into $KU_GCOV_DIR/_merged across every\nmodule the run selects. It then prints one aggregated summary filtered\nto the .c files that triggered a module (headers are skipped, but\nstill available in the full annotated output under $KU_GCOV_DIR).\n\nBy default only the directories of the changed/triggering files are\ncollected, which is quick; -f additionally pulls in every dependency\n.ko's directory for a complete report, but is much slower. The\ngcov-tool merge step itself is skipped whenever there is nothing to\nsum yet, the common case of running on a single uncommitted change.\n\nExample, after changing lustre/lod/lod_lov.c and lod_object.c:\n\n  $ lustre/kunit/ku -g\n  ...\n  --- ku: aggregated gcov summary (changed files only) ---\n      lustre/lod/lod_lov.c                     18.92% of 1395\n      lustre/lod/lod_object.c                  6.02% of 4781\n  ku: -g: full report (all files) saved under /tmp/ku-gcov/_merged\n  ku: all selected kunit modules passed\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:Claude Sonnet 5.0 [Augment Code]\nChange-Id: I18ca317cc345b2ec1d6b59b439f77afcfcf36c35\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
